From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:11:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #4157] mcs51: refuse struct returns that would be
 miscompiled

Functions can return a struct or union only from a plain variable. For
any other expression of struct type (a call, *p, a[i], s.m, a compound
literal, a conditional) the return statement receives the address of the
object. The code generator returned that address in the registers and
never wrote the caller's object, without any diagnostic.

Until returns of such expressions are implemented, report an error that
says how to rewrite the code. This is a temporary measure, not the fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mcs51/gen.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mcs51/gen.c b/src/mcs51/gen.c
index fead30fb7..4c95cfb50 100644
--- a/src/mcs51/gen.c
+++ b/src/mcs51/gen.c
@@ -5485,6 +5485,14 @@ genRet (iCode *ic)
   size = AOP_SIZE (IC_LEFT (ic));
   const bool bigreturn = IS_STRUCT (operandType (IC_LEFT (ic)));
 
+  /* Only a plain variable arrives here as a struct. Any other struct-valued expression (a call,
+     *p, a[i], s.m, a compound literal) arrives as its address, and the code below would return
+     that address in the registers and leave the caller's object untouched (bug #4157). Until
+     such returns are implemented, refuse them instead of generating wrong code silently. */
+  if (!bigreturn && IS_STRUCT (currFunc->type->next))
+    werrorfl (ic->filename, ic->lineno, E_NOT_ALLOWED,
+              "returning this struct or union expression directly (assign it to a variable and return that) is");
+
   if (bigreturn)
     {
       // This needs to match the logic in genFunction - could be factored out, but there is a major rewrite of mcs51 codegen planned anyaway,
